### piped grep with an unquoted leading-star pattern
cat playlist.txt | grep *.mp3
>>> SC2035 1:25
>>> SC2062 1:25
>>> SC2063 1:25

### inverted extended grep with an unquoted star pattern
grep -Ev cow*test barn.txt
>>> SC2022 1:10
>>> SC2062 1:10

### regex option in equals form with an unquoted glob
grep --regex=*.mp3 playlist.m3u
>>> SC2062 1:6

### unquoted star-wrapped pattern
grep *foo* notes.txt
>>> SC2035 1:6
>>> SC2062 1:6
>>> SC2063 1:6

### ls piped into grep with an unquoted pattern
ls | grep foo*.jpg
>>> SC2010 1:1
>>> SC2022 1:11
>>> SC2062 1:11

### glob as file argument is fine
grep foo *.txt
>>> SC2035 1:10

### a command named grep-v is not grep
grep-v --regex *.mp3
>>> SC2035 1:16

### escaped star in the pattern is literal
grep foo\*.mp3 library.txt
>>> SC2022 1:6

### pattern after double dash and glob file
grep -- -verbose bar*
>>> none

### pattern after -e and glob file
grep -e -verbose bar*
>>> none

### pattern after separate regex option and glob file
grep --regex -verbose bar*
>>> none
